(a) that the victim was a married lady (she may also be a 2025.09.01 15:21:19 +0530 SC No. 56587/16 State. Vs. Umed Singh & ORS. Page : 47 of 63 widow);
(b) that she has been subjected to cruelty by her husband or the relatives of husband;
(c) that such cruelty consisted of either (1) harassment of the woman with a view to coerce her for meeting a demand of dowry or (2) a willful conduct by the husband or the relative of the husband of such a nature as is likely to lead the lady to commit suicide or to cause grave injury to her life, limb or health;
(d) that such injury aforesaid may be mental or physical;

In order to bring home the charge of dowry death u/s 304B IPC, it is essential for the prosecution to prove the following ingredients:
(a) that the death of the woman was caused by any burns or bodily injuries or in the circumstances which are not normal;
(b) such death occurs within seven years from the date of marriage;
(c) that the victim was subjected to cruelty or harassment by her POOJA husband or any relative of the husband; TALWAR (d) such cruelty or harassment should be for or in connection Digitally signed by POOJA TALWAR with the demand of dowry; and Date: 2025.09.01 15:21:28 +0530 SC No. 56587/16 State.
